<title>CANADA: Canada body details Prairie Spring Wheat protein.</title>
<headline>Canada body details Prairie Spring Wheat protein.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Canadian Grain Commission on Monday detailed the protein content of Canada Prairie Spring Red Wheat.</p>
<p>			   No1 CPSR</p>
<p>PROVINCE	SAMPLES   MEAN AVG  MIN. MAX. (PCT)</p>
<p>Manitoba	  98	11.5	9.5  16.0</p>
<p>Saskatchewan   166	10.8	8.6  13.6</p>
<p>Alberta	  134	10.8	7.6  15.5</p>
<p>W. Canada	398	11.0	7.6  16.0</p>
<p>			   No2 CPSR</p>
<p>PROVINCE	SAMPLES   MEAN AVG  MIN. MAX. (PCT)</p>
<p>Manitoba	  18	11.5     10.2  12.9</p>
<p>Saskatchewan    74	10.3	7.5  13.7</p>
<p>Alberta	  152	10.2	7.6  13.9</p>
<p>W. Canada	244	10.3	7.5  13.9</p>
<p>			   CW FEED</p>
<p>PROVINCE	SAMPLES   MEAN AVG  MIN. MAX. (PCT)</p>
<p>Manitoba	  16	11.3     10.4  12.4</p>
<p>Saskatchewan     8	10.6	8.8  11.7</p>
<p>Alberta	   64	10.3	8.5  12.9</p>
<p>W. Canada	 88	10.5	8.5  12.9</p>
<p>			   ALL GRADES</p>
<p>PROVINCE	SAMPLES   MEAN AVG  MIN. MAX. (PCT)</p>
<p>Manitoba	 132	11.5	9.5  16.0</p>
<p>Saskatchewan   248	10.7	7.5  13.7</p>
<p>Alberta	  350	10.5	7.6  15.5</p>
<p>W. Canada	730	10.7	7.5  16.0</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras 204 947 3548))</p>
